.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://modgov.waverley.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-10-22","committee":"Landlord Services Advisory Board (Executive Working Group)","time":"10.00 am","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://modgov.waverley.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-11-02","committee":"Executive","time":"7.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://modgov.waverley.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-11-03","committee":"WSC Audit and Governance Committee","time":"2.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://modgov.waverley.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-11-10","committee":"Council","time":"7.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://modgov.waverley.gov.uk"}],"recent":[{"date":"2026-09-08","committee":"Council","time":"7.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://modgov.waverley.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-09-10","committee":"Guildford & Waverley Joint Overview & Scrutiny Committee","time":"7.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://modgov.waverley.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-09-14","committee":"Overview and Scrutiny Committee","time":"7.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://modgov.waverley.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-09-16","committee":"Audit & Risk Committee","time":"7.00 pm","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://modgov.waverley.gov.uk"},{"date":"2026-09-24","committee":"Landlord Services Advisory Board (Executive Working Group)","time":"10.00 am","status":"Confirmed","webcast":false,"url":"https://modgov.waverley.gov.uk"}]},"news":[],"news_drafts":[{"headline":"Restricted government grant reserves are being drawn down, with the Ukraine grant reducing by \u00a3200k and multiple grants fully depleted.","lead":"Depletion of one-time, restricted government funding signals the end of temporary resources; services dependent on these grants will require alternative funding or budget reallocation if they continue.","iso":"2026-09-14","paper_title":"Appendix 6 i","paper_url":"https://modgov.waverley.gov.uk/documents/s77263/77263.pdf","byline":"PWLBintel \u00b7 from committee papers","draft":true},{"headline":"Waverley manages \u00a349.9m in Section 106 and Community Infrastructure Levy commitments with significant budget movements of \u00a338.3m.","lead":"The scale of CIL/S106 commitments reflects capital delivery obligations; large budget movements signal either project acceleration, delivery delays being resolved, or rebalancing that affects infrastructure timelines.","iso":"2026-09-14","paper_title":"Appendix 6 i","paper_url":"https://modgov.waverley.gov.uk/documents/s77263/77263.pdf","byline":"PWLBintel \u00b7 from committee papers","draft":true},{"headline":"The council is committing \u00a31.8m to Local Government Reorganisation implementation costs.","lead":"LGR implementation is an extraordinary cost directly impacting financial capacity; organizational restructuring of this scale could affect financial stability and resource management.","iso":"2026-09-14","paper_title":"Appendix 6 i","paper_url":"https://modgov.waverley.gov.uk/documents/s77263/77263.pdf","byline":"PWLBintel \u00b7 from committee papers","draft":true}],"findings":[{"iso":"2026-09-14","committee":"Overview and Scrutiny Committee","paper_title":"Appendix 6 i","paper_url":"https://modgov.waverley.gov.uk/documents/s77263/77263.pdf","headline":"Restricted government grant reserves are being drawn down, with the Ukraine grant reducing by \u00a3200k and multiple grants fully depleted.","detail":"Ukraine grant reserves falling from \u00a31,920,410 to \u00a31,720,410 with \u00a3200,000 deployed. Simultaneously, multiple restricted grants (Extended producer responsibility \u00a31,673,450, Energy Rebate Council Tax admin \u00a3120,742) are forecasted to reach zero as they are fully spent.","category":"income","matters":"Depletion of one-time, restricted government funding signals the end of temporary resources; services dependent on these grants will require alternative funding or budget reallocation if they continue.","figures":"Ukraine grant: \u00a3200,000 drawn down; Extended producer responsibility: \u00a31,673,450 fully depleted; Energy Rebate: \u00a3120,742 fully depleted","quote":"Ukraine Grant -1,920,410 200,000 -1,720,410","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-14","committee":"Overview and Scrutiny Committee","paper_title":"Appendix 6 i","paper_url":"https://modgov.waverley.gov.uk/documents/s77263/77263.pdf","headline":"Waverley manages \u00a349.9m in Section 106 and Community Infrastructure Levy commitments with significant budget movements of \u00a338.3m.","detail":"The council holds \u00a349,887,278 in restricted CIL and S106 developer contribution funds with substantial budget movements of \u00a338,302,664, indicating either major capital project acceleration or revaluation. Forecast shows \u00a311,584,614 remaining.","category":"capital","matters":"The scale of CIL/S106 commitments reflects capital delivery obligations; large budget movements signal either project acceleration, delivery delays being resolved, or rebalancing that affects infrastructure timelines.","figures":"\u00a349,887,278 opening; \u00a338,302,664 budget movements; \u00a311,584,614 forecast remaining","quote":"Restricted Use CIL & S106 Funds -49,887,278 38,302,664 -11,584,614","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-14","committee":"Overview and Scrutiny Committee","paper_title":"Appendix 6 i","paper_url":"https://modgov.waverley.gov.uk/documents/s77263/77263.pdf","headline":"The council is committing \u00a31.8m to Local Government Reorganisation implementation costs.","detail":"A new reserve of \u00a31,797,783 has been created for LGR implementation, with \u00a31,000,000 forecast remaining for deployment in the year ahead. This represents a major one-off organizational restructuring expense.","category":"governance","matters":"LGR implementation is an extraordinary cost directly impacting financial capacity; organizational restructuring of this scale could affect financial stability and resource management.","figures":"\u00a31,797,783 total allocation; \u00a31,000,000 forecast remaining","quote":"Local Government Reorganisation - Implementation Costs 0 -1,797,783 797,783 0 -1,000,000","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-14","committee":"Overview and Scrutiny Committee","paper_title":"Appendix 7","paper_url":"https://modgov.waverley.gov.uk/documents/s77265/77265.pdf","headline":"Council is responsible for ~\u00a333m of collection fund debts, backed by \u00a32.1m bad debt provision.","detail":"Waverley's share of collection fund debts is approximately \u00a319.8m of council tax arrears and \u00a313m of business rates arrears (\u00a332.8m combined). The council notes a \u00a32.1m bad debt provision to 'mitigate any impact to the general fund', which would cover only 6% of Waverley's total collection fund exposure.","category":"income","matters":"If the \u00a32.1m provision proves insufficient against actual collection fund write-offs, the council will need to draw reserves or make further provisions, impacting its financial flexibility.","figures":"Council tax share: ~\u00a319,843,287; business rates share: ~\u00a312,987,173; provision: \u00a32,100,000","quote":"We have a total Collection Fund bad debt provision of \u00a32.1m for debt to be written off against, this will mitigate any impact to the general fund.","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-14","committee":"Overview and Scrutiny Committee","paper_title":"Appendix 7","paper_url":"https://modgov.waverley.gov.uk/documents/s77265/77265.pdf","headline":"Community Services receivables of \u00a3605k in the 90-180 day band comprise 84% of all debt in that aging category.","detail":"Community Services alone accounts for \u00a3605,305 of the \u00a3720,276 in 90-180 day aged receivables, representing a highly concentrated collection problem in a single service area. This suggests either a specific failure in collections processes for that service, a recent policy change affecting those users' ability to pay, or an underlying affordability crisis in the community service user base.","category":"income","matters":"A concentrated collection problem in one service area may indicate a remediable issue (broken process, policy) but could also signal broader user affordability crises that may spread to other services.","figures":"\u00a3605,305 (84% of \u00a3720,276 total 90-180 day debt)","quote":"Community Services 37,198 605,305 20 132 642,656","material":true}],"editorial":null,"freshness":{"last_paper_iso":"2026-09-14"},"name":"Waverley","daily_post":{"iso":"2026-09-26","since_iso":"2026-08-27","distress":false,"headline":"Restricted government grant reserves are being drawn down, with the Ukraine grant reducing by \u00a3200k and multiple grants fully depleted.","lead":"Depletion of one-time, restricted government funding signals the end of temporary resources; services dependent on these grants will require alternative funding or budget reallocation if they continue.","also":["32 other findings in this window"],"watch":"Executive on 2026-10-06","n_findings":33,"n_documents":0,"top_paper_title":"Appendix 6 i","top_paper_url":"https://modgov.waverley.gov.uk/documents/s77263/77263.pdf","draft":true},"findings_total":84,"news_drafts_total":3}}